---
/* =========================================================================
   ABOUT
   ⚠ ALL PROSE IN THIS FILE IS PLACEHOLDER COPY. See PLACEHOLDERS.md.
   Written at roughly the right length so you can judge the layout.
   ========================================================================= */

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/site/PageHeader.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/site/ContactBlock.astro';
import { cvDownload } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Background, research interests, and community work."
>
  <div class="container">
    <PageHeader
      eyebrow="About"
      title="A researcher and training designer working on community resilience"
      lede="I am interested in the difference between a community that has a plan and a community that can actually act — and in what kinds of learning close that gap."
    />
  </div>

  <div class="container about">
    <div class="about__body prose">
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] I grew up in Northern California and have spent most of my
        working life within a few hours of where I started, which turns out to
        matter for this kind of work. The communities I study are ones I have
        some standing in, and the questions I ask tend to come from something I
        watched happen rather than something I read.
      </p>

      <h2>Professional background</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] Several paragraphs about your professional trajectory —
        where you have worked, what kinds of roles you have held, and what the
        through-line is. This is the section people read when deciding whether
        to get in touch, so it should be specific rather than comprehensive.
      </p>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] Where work has been carried out for a specific employer,
        this is the natural place to say so plainly, and to distinguish that work
        from the personal projects and prototypes elsewhere on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>Academic background</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] Degrees, institutions, and the shape of your training —
        written as narrative rather than as a list. The list already exists on
        the <a href="/cv">CV</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Research interests</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] What you are actually curious about, stated as questions
        rather than as fields. Two or three paragraphs.
      </p>

      <h2>Disaster resilience and community work</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] The applied side: coalitions, volunteer work, advisory
        roles, and the ongoing relationships that keep the research honest.
      </p>

      <h2>Teaching and training</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] Your approach to teaching and facilitation, and how it
        connects to the work in the <a href="/training">Training Lab</a>. This is
        a good place to say what you believe about adult learning, briefly and
        without jargon.
      </p>

      <h2>Writing</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] What you write, where it appears, and why. Link through to
        the <a href="/writing">archive</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Beyond the work</h2>
      <p>
        [PLACEHOLDER] A short, genuine paragraph — the outdoors, a craft, a
        river, whatever is true. One paragraph is plenty; it does more for the
        human register of a site like this than three would.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="about__aside">
      <div class="about__portrait">
        <!-- Replace with a real portrait at /public/images/portrait.jpg -->
        <div class="about__portrait-placeholder" aria-hidden="true">
          <span>Portrait</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <dl class="about__facts">
        <dt>Based in</dt>
        <dd>[PLACEHOLDER] Chico, California</dd>

        <dt>Works on</dt>
        <dd>Community resilience, disaster preparedness, learning design</dd>

        <dt>Currently</dt>
        <dd>[PLACEHOLDER] Your current position and affiliation</dd>
      </dl>

      <p class="about__cv">
        <a class="button button--secondary" href={cvDownload} download>
          Download CV (PDF)
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ContactBlock />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-2xl);
    align-items: start;
  }

  @media (min-width: 60rem) {
    .about {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16rem;
      gap: var(--space-2xl);
    }

    .about__aside {
      position: sticky;
      top: var(--space-lg);
      order: 2;
    }
  }

  .about__body { max-width: var(--width-prose); }

  .about__portrait-placeholder {
    aspect-ratio: 4 / 5;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--color-paper-sunk);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caps);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
  }

  .about__facts {
    margin-top: var(--space-md);
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }

  .about__facts dt {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-caps);
    color: var(--color-ink-faint);
    margin-top: var(--space-sm);
  }

  .about__facts dd {
    margin: var(--space-3xs) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-ink-muted);
    line-height: var(--leading-normal);
  }

  .about__cv { margin-top: var(--space-lg); }
</style>
